[h2]Compact console update[/h2]
Added a shared compact console shell with fixed navigation/actions, independent viewports and a narrow-screen Back layout. Existing panels and native instrument dimensions are not globally resized. Separated Orders, Crew & Training and Time-skip. Equipment-specific forms use drafts, complete form validation, stale rejection, Apply/Discard and explicit Resume after changing enabled orders. Disabled and manual-stop states remain intact. Added searchable storage/connection pickers, opt-in nicknames, native artwork with neutral placeholders, and an input-isolated ship picker with overlap disambiguation. Native names, object IDs and physical inventories are unchanged.
[b]Prepared, not published. Unity gameplay and scale evaluation remain owner-run.[/b]
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/control-panel-guide.md]Console controls, drafts and owner checks[/url]

[h1]Phobos Framework[/h1]
[h2]Trimmed-grid save correction in 0.24.1[/h2]
Synchronizes outgoing saved dimensions after native grid trimming and validates already-affected headers against their exterior boundary and saved room positions. Corrects the inspected Ostranauts 1.0.1.5 save-order defect before Shipbreaker's grid guard runs. Room IDs, atmosphere, zones, items and construction progress are retained; original archives are not edited. Ambiguous records remain untouched. Both reported archives pass offline checks; gameplay confirmation of this third fix is pending.
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/shipbreaker-room-load-mitigation.md]Evidence, limits and reload instructions[/url]
[h2]Saved construction-marker health in 0.23.1[/h2]
Corrects the inspected Ostranauts 1.0.1.5 loader's zero-health comparison for living saved construction markers with recorded remaining health. Retains original damage and construction progress for verified vanilla and available mod targets. No free repairs or resurrection of destroyed equipment. Keep Shipbreaker 0.19.1+ for its separate saved-grid guard. The owner confirmed the reported wear-related reload worked; the later stale-header case is addressed separately in 0.24.1.
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/shipbreaker-room-load-mitigation.md]Evidence, limits and reload check[/url]
[h2]Solar-system economy in 0.23.0[/h2]
Shared verified vanilla retail endpoint lookup and additive regional offers. Missing optional kiosks are reported and skipped without redirecting stock or disabling content. Consumers retain ownership of balance; native market pricing and inventories remain authoritative.
Shared service for content mods. Authored availability follows native economic roles; native supply/demand, merchant terms and restocking remain in control. No new settlements, guaranteed stock or live-price promises. Prepared offline, not gameplay-validated or published.
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/solar-system-economy.md]Regional coverage, sources and limits[/url]
[h2]Native instrument display correction in 0.21.2[/h2]
Restores the donor-audit path for native knobs, switches and sliders when BepInEx loads the game assembly from memory. The same pinned game hash and isolated component checks remain required. Shared fixed-field typography supports Auto Nav's compact labels without shrinking text or changing shared fonts. Prepared offline; visual and native-interaction confirmation remain pending.
[h2]Saved-grid support in 0.21.1[/h2]
Provides the checked bounds calculation used by Shipbreaker 0.19.1 to mitigate room misassignment during pending-equipment reloads. The grid-restoration hook belongs to Shipbreaker; Framework 0.23.1 adds the separate marker-health correction above. No saved records are rewritten. The owner reported a successful first affected-save reload on 26 September 2026; the later wear-related recurrence required this follow-up.
[h2]Shared completion cues[/h2]
One optional quiet completion channel now supports watched D4/R4 batches, meals, whole-crop readiness and finite navigation arrivals. Volume/mute and burst suppression apply across the suite. Original procedural audio; no native recordings copied. No saved watch replay. Gameplay/listening review pending.
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/shared-completion-cues.md]Supported events and shared controls[/url]
[b]Version:[/b] 0.26.0
[b]Publication status:[/b] Not published - development candidate

Shared foundations for the Phobos Ostranauts mods and other mod authors. Install this alongside a content mod; Framework does not add a complete gameplay activity on its own.

[h2]Current features[/h2]
[list]
[*]Native construction, maintenance, additive merchant stock and material accounting.
[*]Versioned saved state, physical transfers, explicit endpoint pairing and ship-scoped equipment controls.
[*]Measured power and liquid delivery, shared conduit routes, finite solution accounting and optional provider adapters.
[*]Translation lookup, reusable native instruments and opt-in Phobos Scope performance recording.
[*]Shared native INSTALL category validation supports content equipment in the existing PDA tabs.
[/list]

[h2]Limits and save behaviour[/h2]
[list]
[*]This is an experimental shared library. Successful offline checks do not establish in-game compatibility.
[*]Phobos Scope recording is disabled by default. The recorder is bundled; no Rust process is needed during play.
[/list]

[h2]Requirements and installation[/h2]
Ostranauts 1.0.1.5 and BepInEx 5 (inspected baseline 5.4.23.5). No Shipbreaker, Crafting Framework or Salvage Workshop dependency.

This is a maintained pre-publication page draft, not a download announcement. No Workshop item has been published for this draft. Use the installation guide for source/prepared-package availability and loader setup. Do not remove required providers from saves that contain their content.

