[h2]Fluid network update[/h2]
Bounded multi-receiver port banks retain the original single-pair identity. Reusable retained two-component fluid lines preserve cargo, route binding and transit clocks across reloads.

[h2]Equipment and item reference[/h2]
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/framework-item-reference.md]Read this mod’s item reference[/url] for functions, use, acquisition and applicable base prices, repair and salvage. Generated tables follow the current source candidate; proposals and prototype limitations are labelled.

[h2]Nutrient recovery and optional wet-reject collection[/h2]
Optional Agriculture 0.9.0 integration reuses the original Residue Collector with finite capacity, exclusive pairing and its existing mount requirements. Framework 0.22.0 and Shipbreaker 0.20.0 support measured wet-reject capture from [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3757331189]Valtora’s Ship’s Water 0.16.1[/url]. Full or unavailable linked collectors hold wastewater in its source tank. No wastewater-to-fertilizer recipe is claimed. [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/agriculture-nutrient-production.md]Operating guide, economic limits and research attribution[/url].

[h2]Panel feedback[/h2]
Framework 0.24.2 shares a presentation-only rule used by Agriculture 0.11.1 and Shipbreaker 0.24.1 to avoid echoing successful status paragraphs or notices already shown in live readouts. Errors and distinct action responses remain visible. No gameplay state or console output changes. Prepared offline; visual confirmation pending.

[h2]Bulk merchant stock[/h2]
Quantity-aware merchant and regional-stock overloads request bounded physical lots while retaining the old single-unit API. Probability and stock condition remain independent; native and third-party branches and existing inventories are preserved.
Normal restocking is required; updating does not refill existing shops. [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/merchant-stock.md]Current quantities and restocking guide[/url]. Prepared candidate; in-game stock/capacity review pending.

[h2]Crew roster correction[/h2]
Framework 0.25.1 fixes repeated CrewWork.Poll null exceptions by using the native company roster for work discovery, crew controls and time-skip preview. Missing or unloaded crew do not block other workers; departure still requires every roster member aboard. Saved orders and training are preserved. Automated regression checks are not gameplay validation.

[h2]Crew standing orders[/h2]
Added default-disabled standing orders, native task publication, exact worker context, equipment/input/capacity reservations, per-crew permissions and shared roster/equipment/C1 controls. Added persistent specialities and powered-terminal study; completed practice and study combine toward authored 20-hour/10-hour thresholds, with a 20% hands-on duration benefit. Existing terminal actions are retained. Added bounded native time-skip coordination, checked travel/handling budgets, measured machine ticks and repair-time sharing. Native rest, care, events, payroll and fuel remain native; exterior operations suspend. Saved manual stops and routine resume preferences remain authoritative. Unknown saved records are retained and blocked.
Native method/definition and offline checks are not in-game validation. Common Sense integration uses native tasks; live compatibility and UI review remain owner-run.
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/crew-automation.md]Crew controls, time-skip limits and owner checks[/url]. Optional native-task coexistence with [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3789049955]LOGUSS’s Common Sense modules[/url]; added study preserves [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3788237703]jossla’s Study at Terminals[/url].
